Ticket #4471 contains two problems. The intake tags and subject lines do not reliably separate
them; the tenant's locale, booking form, and report channel do.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Shared parser

The shared parser reads every date month first. For tenants whose locale writes the day first,
the month and day are swapped. This affects app and email reports, plus form reports that do not
come through booking-v3's month-first hint.

## Booking-v3 hint

Booking-v3 displays `MM/DD/YYYY`. People follow that hint, but day-first tenants interpret the
submitted value in their locale's order. These form reports need a separate fix from the shared
parser.

<Callout>
Split #4471 by computed cause, not by subject or intake tag. Keep one engineering ticket for each
row in the table.
</Callout>

